WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.285 --> 00:00:06.208
What if my word doesn't match my company's word?

00:00:06.714 --> 00:00:08.840
So I got a great question, a number of times.

00:00:09.069 --> 00:00:10.473
The first time it came up was in Malaysia

00:00:10.663 --> 00:00:11.557
when I was doing the conference.

00:00:12.589 --> 00:00:14.911
I believe that everybody has one word that connects them

00:00:15.345 --> 00:00:16.601
that defines them.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:19.200
It’s a one word biography and when you figure out what that one word is

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.644
it helps make all decisions in your life a lot easier.

00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:23.869
It helps your marketing decisions easier

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:25.617
it helps partnership decisions easier

00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:27.035
every decision in your business

00:00:27.035 --> 00:00:27.952
and in your life becomes easier

00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:29.378
when you know what you stand for

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:30.956
So mine is BELIEVE

00:00:32.503 --> 00:00:36.007
and when I’m creating new content for my website

00:00:36.186 --> 00:00:37.154
for Twitter, for Facebook

00:00:37.384 --> 00:00:38.286
when I’m making these videos

00:00:38.673 --> 00:00:39.838
it has to be about believe

00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:42.933
because that’s who I am and it makes me happy

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:45.294
and it makes me excited and it drives me.

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:47.649
You know, I want to see what I create

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:48.776
and say “I’m proud of that”

00:00:49.029 --> 00:00:50.878
and not just be creating it to try

00:00:50.914 --> 00:00:51.737
to get lots of views.

00:00:52.106 --> 00:00:53.866
I actually like everything that I’m making.

00:00:55.525 --> 00:00:58.270
So I got a question in Malaysia

00:00:58.513 --> 00:00:59.336
at the conference somebody asked

00:00:59.516 --> 00:01:00.384
“You know, what if, you know

00:01:00.384 --> 00:01:02.277
so I’m working on a… I work at a company

00:01:02.503 --> 00:01:04.230
and I’m working on their social media campaign

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:05.795
but what if, you know

00:01:05.795 --> 00:01:07.330
my word doesn’t match the company’s word?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.196
What do I do?”

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.011
And it’s a tough question.

00:01:10.185 --> 00:01:12.043
You know, I don’t like giving advice to employees

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.414
because I usually end up making them become entrepreneurs

00:01:14.571 --> 00:01:17.595
but what I would advise you to do

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.049
when you’re thinking about working with other people

00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:22.936
you may not always find everybody

00:01:23.018 --> 00:01:24.938
has exactly the same word on your team

00:01:25.134 --> 00:01:26.393
or in your circle at the job you’re at.

00:01:26.602 --> 00:01:28.923
So for example, mine is BELIEVE.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.850
Jason who does a lot of work with me

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:33.205
his word is RISE.

00:01:34.739 --> 00:01:36.453
Rich who does a lot of work with me

00:01:36.661 --> 00:01:37.682
his word is INSPIRE.

00:01:38.148 --> 00:01:39.617
And so, these are not

00:01:39.814 --> 00:01:42.233
it’s not exactly BELIEVE but they’re sister words, right.

00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:43.701
That’s the reason why I can get along with them

00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:46.462
because they have words that are not exactly the same

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:47.577
but very complementary.

00:01:47.981 --> 00:01:49.886
And so if you’re working at a company

00:01:50.146 --> 00:01:52.145
and your word is very complementary to

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.431
what the company stands for

00:01:53.431 --> 00:01:54.589
then it’s going to be a good fit

00:01:54.589 --> 00:01:55.767
you know, you’re going to be happy there

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.441
you’re going to like the people there

00:01:57.441 --> 00:01:59.394
you’re going to able to create marketing campaigns

00:01:59.394 --> 00:02:01.361
that will mean something and be important.

00:02:01.911 --> 00:02:02.749
If you’re working at a company

00:02:02.749 --> 00:02:04.270
that doesn’t stand for anything

00:02:04.592 --> 00:02:06.561
or whose values are not aligned with you

00:02:06.824 --> 00:02:08.028
or whose one word doesn’t match

00:02:08.592 --> 00:02:11.517
is not even close to what yours is then you’re, you know

00:02:11.679 --> 00:02:13.778
probably not going to have a good time

00:02:14.081 --> 00:02:15.278
working at that company

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.717
And you know, no marketing plan is going to save you

00:02:18.898 --> 00:02:20.526
and you’d be better off finding a different company

00:02:20.526 --> 00:02:21.768
that does match your values

00:02:22.548 --> 00:02:24.206
or starting your own thing, you know.

00:02:24.465 --> 00:02:27.162
My voice is jumping all over the place.

00:02:27.388 --> 00:02:28.258
I’m sick as a dog

00:02:28.485 --> 00:02:29.226
I’m running a fever.

00:02:29.598 --> 00:02:31.051
Anyway, this is important.

00:02:31.051 --> 00:02:31.924
I wanted to get it out.

00:02:33.861 --> 00:02:36.541
So that’s my advice if you’re word does not match your company’s word.

00:02:36.897 --> 00:02:37.556
Believe.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.202
For those of you watching, you liked the video

00:02:39.202 --> 00:02:39.798
thumbs-up below.

00:02:40.184 --> 00:02:42.681
Let me know what you think. Leave a comment underneath.

00:02:42.886 --> 00:02:45.146
You can wish me to feel better if you want.

00:02:45.341 --> 00:02:47.314
If you have a question, put it there. I’ll respond.

00:02:47.314 --> 00:02:49.114
And you can click on my face

00:02:49.114 --> 00:02:49.955
to subscribe to the channel.

00:02:50.154 --> 00:02:52.445
Thank you so much and I’ll see you soon.

